## Day 3 Summary (May 9)

| Command / Action              | Correct Command / Meaning                     | Use / Example                                   | Notes |
|-------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------|-------|
| Install VS Code               | Install .deb package                          | sudo dpkg -i code_*.deb                         | Use sudo or run as root |
| Open Firefox                  | Launch Firefox browser                        | firefox                                         | firefox google.com |
| dpkg                          | Install .deb packages                         | sudo dpkg -i filename.deb                       | Manual package installer |
| chmod +x                      | Make file executable                          | chmod +x filename.sh                            | Required to run scripts/programs |
| apt install                   | Install software from repositories            | sudo apt install vlc                            | Most common installation method |
| snap                          | Ubuntu package manager                        | sudo snap install package-name                  | Easy modern way to install apps |
| wget                          | Download file from internet                   | wget https://example.com/file.deb               | Web get command |
| code .                        | Open VS Code in current directory             | code .                                          | Very useful shortcut |
| history                       | Show previous commands                        | history                                         | See command history |
| apt-get purge                 | Completely uninstall software                 | sudo apt-get purge vlc                          | Removes program + configuration files |
| Tab Key                       | Auto-complete                                 | Type few letters + Press Tab                    | Saves time while typing |

### Day 3 Key Learnings
- Linux is great for troubleshooting and installing software.
- `chmod +x` is important to make any file or script executable.
- `dpkg` is used for installing `.deb` files (like VS Code).
- `apt install` is the standard way to install most programs.
- `snap` is another easy package manager in Ubuntu.
- Always use `sudo` when installing or uninstalling software.

